From aab08c677ee9e7477a72e515e309bfdc4f106198 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yann Gautier <yann.gautier@foss.st.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Mar 2026 16:05:56 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 434/572] fix(stm32mp2): check index before accessing the PM
 tables

In stm32_parse_domain_idle_state(), there are 2 loops for which we check
the table value at an index before checking the index itself. Switch
the index check and the table value check.
While at it, add parentheses around the 2 checks.
This was found by Coverity: Defect (reverse_overrun)

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [ST downstream https://github.com/STMicroelectronics/arm-trusted-firmware.git 59ead3c8797947cd845d1dc8d3bb9e334ee37896 fix(stm32mp2): check index before accessing the PM tables]
Change-Id: I68b5eba48bfa9cd5c8d882eafecf7cd37509e03d
Signed-off-by: Yann Gautier <yann.gautier@foss.st.com>
Reviewed-on: https://gerrit.st.com/c/mpu/oe/st/tf-a/+/545849
ACI: CIBUILD <MDG-smet-aci-builds@list.st.com>
ACI: CITOOLS <MDG-smet-aci-reviews@list.st.com>
Domain-Review: Patrick DELAUNAY <patrick.delaunay@foss.st.com>
Reviewed-by: Maxime MERE <maxime.mere@foss.st.com>
---
 plat/st/stm32mp2/stm32mp2_pm.c | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/plat/st/stm32mp2/stm32mp2_pm.c b/plat/st/stm32mp2/stm32mp2_pm.c
index f2ec3b6167..9c19411cd9 100644
--- a/plat/st/stm32mp2/stm32mp2_pm.c
+++ b/plat/st/stm32mp2/stm32mp2_pm.c
@@ -1540,7 +1540,7 @@ static int stm32_parse_domain_idle_state(void *fdt)
 
 	/* Add each supported power state with same order than stm32mp_pm_idle_states */
 	for (j = 0U; stm32mp_pm_idle_states[j] != 0U; j++) {
-		for (i = 0U; i < PM_IDLE_STATES_SIZE && domain_idle_states[i] != 0U ; i++) {
+		for (i = 0U; (i < PM_IDLE_STATES_SIZE) && (domain_idle_states[i] != 0U); i++) {
 			if (domain_idle_states[i] == stm32mp_pm_idle_states[j]) {
 				stm32mp_supported_pwr_states[nb_states++] = domain_idle_states[i];
 				break;
@@ -1549,7 +1549,7 @@ static int stm32_parse_domain_idle_state(void *fdt)
 	}
 
 	/* Add STANDBY at the end of the list if supported */
-	for (i = 0U; i < PM_IDLE_STATES_SIZE && domain_idle_states[i] != 0U ; i++) {
+	for (i = 0U; (i < PM_IDLE_STATES_SIZE) && (domain_idle_states[i] != 0U); i++) {
 		if (domain_idle_states[i] == PWRSTATE_STANDBY) {
 			stm32mp_supported_pwr_states[nb_states++] = PWRSTATE_STANDBY;
 			break;
-- 
2.53.0

